<title>BELGIUM: ActivCard lowers Easdaq IPO price.</title>
<headline>ActivCard lowers Easdaq IPO price.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>French smart card maker ActivCard SA said on Saturday it had modified the terms of its initial public offering on Easdaq, Europe's new small cap market.</p>
<p>In a notice published in Belgian newspapers, ActivCard said the indicative price for the IPO was lowered to $8-$10 from $10-$12 originally and the offer would also be extended until December 16. The final issue price would be announced after the close of the issue on December 16.</p>
<p>ActivCard's issue of three million shares is being managed by French brokerage Hambrecht &amp; Quist Saint Dominique, Belgium's KB Securities and Beeson Gregory of the U.K.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
